{% doc %}
  Outputs the color (lowercase) a media belongs to, read from its alt text, or nothing for a neutral media.
  Alts follow "LELON X — Couleur — Vue n"; free alts such as "LELON ÉLÉA Cognac porté" also work.
  "et" is read as "&" so "Beige et Cognac" matches the "Beige & Cognac" option. Longest match wins.
  The gallery prints the result in data-media-color, which lelon.js reads when the color changes.

  @param {string} alt - Media alt text.
  @param {string[]} colors - Values of the product color option.
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign haystack = alt | downcase | replace: ' et ', ' & '
  assign found = ''
  for color in colors
    assign needle = color | downcase
    if haystack contains needle
      if needle.size > found.size
        assign found = needle
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  echo found
-%}
